+5. Four fixed zero-start unpreconditioned CG candidates: first perpendicular/opposite even systems, then their fully assembled odd sources. At most256 iterations each; fresh action and two exact scans at16,32,...,256. Ordinary CG dot/axpy results generate candidates only. Any nonfinite value or p^T A p<=0 is a preserved breakdown under the frozen protocol, not a reason to extend/restart or change method. Do not use recursive residual as the certificate. Stop only on the first scheduled passing certificate, with fixed first1e-10 and second1e-9 thresholds and final Echi<=1e-6.
